<title>INDIA: India Colgate 6-mth ended March net up.</title>
<headline>India Colgate 6-mth ended March net up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six-months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		356.6  vs	354.0</p>
<p>    Net Sales	     4,677.4  vs    4,279.7</p>
<p>    Other income	    101.6   vs    108.0</p>
<p>    Expenditure	   4,066.3   vs  3,656.1</p>
<p>    Interest		    0.2   vs	3.1</p>
<p>    Depreciation	     61.3   vs     66.8</p>
<p>    Tax			 294.6   vs    307.7</p>
<p>Note: Colgate Palmolive Ltd said its net sales for the year ended March 31, 1997 registered an increase of 13 percent.</p>
<p>The company said it absorbed an amount of approximately 100 million rupees being the differential duty on excise paid inventories after a decision to pass on full benefit of excise duties reductions offered in the 1997/1998 budget. As a result of this, the company's net profit was affected, it said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
